module beadFocusingQC
module ctcDetection

manifest PBS
manifest BSA_Solution
manifest Ethanol70
manifest SheathBuffer
manifest RBCLysisBuffer
manifest QCBeadSuspension
manifest LysedBloodSample
manifest Paraformaldehyde
manifest TritonX100
manifest PanCK_FITC_Antibody
manifest CD45_APC_Antibody
manifest HoechstDye

// ============================================================
// Ultra-fast, label-free isolation of circulating tumor cells
// from blood using spiral microfluidics.
// Warkiani, Khoo, Wu, Tay, Bhagat, Han, Lim
// Nature Protocols, Vol. 11, No. 1, pp. 134-148 (2016)
// DOI: 10.1038/nprot.2016.003
//
// Platform: spiral inertial microfluidic biochip (PDMS/glass).
// Channel dimensions: 500 um wide x 170 um deep, two-loop
// spiral, radius ~10 mm, two inlets (sample outer / sheath
// inner), two outlets (CTC inner / waste outer).
// Inlet split: 75 um sample / 425 um sheath.
// Outlet split: 150 um CTC collection / 350 um waste.
// Operating flow rates: sample 100 uL/min; sheath 750 uL/min
// (single chip). Multiplexed 3x chip: sheath 2100 uL/min.
//
// Separation physics: combined inertial lift force (FL) and
// Dean drag force (FD) in a curvilinear microchannel. CTCs
// (>15 um) focus near the inner wall; RBCs, WBCs, platelets
// (<15 um) migrate along Dean vortices toward outer wall.
// Dean number De = Re * sqrt(DH / 2*RC).
//
// Sample: 7.5 mL whole blood lysed with ammonium chloride RBC
// lysis buffer, resuspended 2x concentrated (~14e6 nucleated
// cells/mL in 3.75 mL PBS) before spiral processing.
// Throughput: 7.5 mL in 37.5 min (single), 12.5 min (3x).
// Performance: >=85% CTC recovery; 99.99% WBC depletion.
//
// NOTE ON FABRICATION ABSTRACTION: Steps 1-19 of the paper
// cover photolithography, DRIE, silanization, PDMS casting,
// soft lithography, and plasma bonding. These are off-chip
// physical fabrication steps that produce the spiral device.
// They are abstracted in BB1 as chip priming operations,
// consistent with BioScript conventions for prior protocols
// in this library. The first on-chip liquid handling step is
// chip priming (Step 20 onward in the paper procedure).
//
// NOTE ON SHEATH/SAMPLE DUAL-INLET: The spiral biochip has
// two independent inlets (sheath buffer inner, sample outer).
// BioScript `mix` abstracts the co-flow merging event at the
// spiral inlet where the two streams combine hydrodynamically.
// This is not a DMF droplet merge; it represents the inertial
// focusing run where sheath and sample enter the spiral channel
// together. The separation occurs passively along the channel
// length via inertial and Dean forces.
//
// NOTE ON QC BEAD CHECK: Step 27 in the paper runs 3-6 um
// polystyrene bead suspension (0.1% v/v) through the primed
// device to confirm particle focusing behavior before patient
// sample processing. The beadFocusingQC module abstracts the
// high-speed camera / phase-contrast microscope readout at
// the outlet region (inner wall focus = pass).
//
// NOTE ON IMMUNOFLUORESCENCE: Staining targets three markers:
//   pan-CK (FITC) -- epithelial marker; CTC positive
//   CD45 (APC)    -- leukocyte marker; CTC negative
//   Hoechst       -- nuclear stain; all nucleated cells
// Putative CTCs: pan-CK+, CD45-, Hoechst+, round nuclei,
// high nuclear-to-cytoplasmic ratio.
// Detection threshold (negative control): >7 CK+ cells/sample.
// ctcDetection module abstracts the fluorescence enumeration
// readout (Olympus IX71/81, ET460/50m / ET535/50m / ET605/70m
// filter set, automated MetaMorph stage scan, ImageJ threshold).
//
// NOTE ON DURATIONS: BioScript duration tokens are `s` and `m`
// only. All hour-based incubations are converted to minutes.
//   5 min priming      = 5m
//   10 min lysis       = 10m
//   37.5 min run       = 37m (single spiral, 7.5 mL lysed blood)
//   30-60 min staining = 30m (antibody incubation on ice)
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main           -- chip priming, bead QC, blood prep,
//                          spiral processing, cell collection
//   BB2  beadPass       -- beadSignal > 0: correct focusing,
//                          proceed to blood processing; dispose
//   BB3  beadFail       -- beadSignal <= 0: focusing incorrect
//                          (wrong channel depth or flow rate);
//                          drain bead suspension, abort run
//   BB4  beadJoin       -- join: blood prep and staining branch
//   BB5  ctcPass        -- ctcSignal > 0: CTC enumeration valid
//                          (>7 pan-CK+ cells); dispose all
//   BB6  ctcFail        -- ctcSignal <= 0: no CTCs detected
//                          (below threshold); drain stained cells
//   BB7  finalCleanup   -- terminal: dispose QC signal, end
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// CHIP PRIMING - STEP 1 (Paper Steps 20-22): Sterilize the
//   primed spiral biochip by flowing 70% (v/v) ethanol in
//   sterile deionized water for 5 min at 750 uL/min to
//   remove air bubbles and sterilize the channel interior.
//   Required for downstream cell culture applications.
//   NOTE: Chip fabrication (Steps 1-19: photolithography,
//   DRIE, silanization, PDMS soft lithography, plasma bonding)
//   is performed off-chip and is not encoded here.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ethanolPrime = dispense 1 units of Ethanol70
channelWash  = mix ethanolPrime with ethanolPrime for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// CHIP PRIMING - STEP 2 (Paper Steps 23-25): Flush residual
//   ethanol and coat microchannel surfaces with sheath buffer
//   (1x sterile PBS + 0.5% w/v BSA) at 750 uL/min for 5 min.
//   BSA coating minimises non-specific cell adhesion to the
//   PDMS channel walls during spiral processing.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bsaSolution    = dispense 1 units of BSA_Solution
sheathPriming  = dispense 1 units of SheathBuffer
surfaceCoating = mix bsaSolution with sheathPriming for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// CHIP PRIMING - STEP 3 (Paper Step 26): Inspect for bubbles
//   using inverted microscope (bright-field mode). Increasing
//   sheath flow rate dislodges residual air pockets.
//   Model as an additional sheath buffer flush.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sheathFlush    = dispense 1 units of SheathBuffer
bubbleRemoval  = mix surfaceCoating with sheathFlush for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// QC BEAD CHECK (Paper Step 27): Load 3-6 um polystyrene bead
//   suspension (0.1% v/v) at 100 uL/min (sample inlet, outer
//   wall) co-flowing with sheath buffer at 750 uL/min (inner
//   inlet). Observe particle distribution across channel width
//   at outlet using phase-contrast microscope + high-speed
//   camera (VisionResearch Phantom v9).
//   Pass criterion: 6 um beads undergo complete Dean cycle
//   (inner -> outer wall migration visible); 15 um beads focus
//   tightly near inner wall at outlet.
//   NOTE: `mix` abstracts the co-flow hydrodynamic event at
//   the spiral inlet (not a DMF electrode merge).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

beadSuspension = dispense 1 units of QCBeadSuspension
sheathQC       = dispense 1 units of SheathBuffer
beadRun        = mix beadSuspension with sheathQC for 5m

beadSignal     = detect beadFocusingQC on beadRun for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Bead focusing QC gate
// Pass (BB2): beadSignal > 0 -> correct particle focusing
//             confirmed (channel depth 165-170 um verified);
//             dispose bead run and proceed to blood processing.
// Fail (BB3): beadSignal <= 0 -> incorrect focusing (channel
//             depth out of tolerance, <160 or >170 um due to
//             improper DRIE); drain, abort run, fabricate new
//             master mold (Table 1, Step 27 troubleshooting).
// Both branches converge at BB4 (beadJoin).
// ============================================================

if (beadSignal > 0) {
    dispose beadRun
} else {
    drain beadRun
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: beadJoin
// Dispose bead focusing QC signal. Control falls into the
// blood preparation and spiral processing branch.
// ============================================================

dispose beadSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// BLOOD PREPARATION - STEP 1 (Paper Steps 28-29): Lyse RBCs
//   using 3x ammonium chloride RBC lysis buffer at 1:3 v/v
//   ratio. Invert conical tube to mix. Incubate 10 min at
//   room temperature (24-26 C) on shaking platform until
//   sample color changes to dark red (complete lysis).
//   NOTE: If spiking with cancer cell lines, cancer cells
//   must be added before lysis step (Reagent Setup in paper).
//   Lysis substantially reduces untargeted blood cells,
//   mitigating cell-cell interactions that impair inertial
//   focusing. Total cell loss from lysis + centrifugation <8%.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rbcLysisBuffer = dispense 1 units of RBCLysisBuffer
lysedBlood1    = dispense 1 units of LysedBloodSample
lysisReaction  = mix lysedBlood1 with rbcLysisBuffer for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// BLOOD PREPARATION - STEP 2 (Paper Step 29): Pellet nucleated
//   cells by centrifugation at 1000g for 5 min at room temp.
//   Resuspend pellet in 1x PBS to 2x concentrated sample
//   (~14e6 nucleated cells/mL; 7.5 mL blood -> 3.75 mL PBS).
//   Model centrifugation as a heat step at room temperature.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pbsResuspend   = dispense 1 units of PBS
heat lysisReaction at 25c for 5m
resuspendedSample = mix lysisReaction with pbsResuspend for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// SPIRAL PROCESSING (Paper Steps 32-37): Co-flow lysed blood
//   (100 uL/min, outer sample inlet) with sheath buffer
//   (750 uL/min, inner sheath inlet) through the two-loop
//   spiral biochip. CTCs (>15 um) focus near the inner wall
//   via inertial lift (FL) overcoming Dean drag (FD); smaller
//   blood cells (RBCs, WBCs, platelets, <15 um) exit from
//   the outer waste outlet following Dean vortex streamlines.
//   Total run: ~37 min for 7.5 mL lysed blood (single chip);
//   <13 min for 3x multiplexed chip (sheath 2100 uL/min).
//   CTC fraction collected from inner outlet into 15 mL tube.
//   NOTE: `mix` abstracts the hydrodynamic co-flow separation
//   event in the spiral channel. The CTCs continuously exit
//   from the inner outlet during this step; this is not a
//   discrete droplet merge but a continuous flow separation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sheathRun      = dispense 1 units of SheathBuffer
spiralRun      = mix resuspendedSample with sheathRun for 37m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// CELL CONCENTRATION (Paper Step 38): Centrifuge collected CTC
//   fraction at 300g for 3 min at room temperature to pellet
//   cells and remove excess volume before staining.
//   Resuspend in ~250 uL PBS for downstream immunostaining.
//   Model centrifugation as a heat step at room temperature.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat spiralRun at 25c for 3m
pbsResuspend2       = dispense 1 units of PBS
concentratedCells   = mix spiralRun with pbsResuspend2 for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// IMMUNOFLUORESCENCE - STEP 1 (Paper Step 40): Fix cells with
//   4% w/v paraformaldehyde (PFA) in PBS for 10 min at room
//   temperature. PFA crosslinks cellular proteins to preserve
//   morphology and antigen epitopes for antibody staining.
//   CAUTION: PFA is a suspected carcinogen; handle with PPE.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pfaFixative  = dispense 1 units of Paraformaldehyde
fixedCells   = mix concentratedCells with pfaFixative for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// IMMUNOFLUORESCENCE - STEP 2 (Paper Step 41): Wash fixed
//   cells with 1-2 mL PBS + 0.5% w/v BSA, centrifuge at
//   300g for 3 min at room temperature to remove residual PFA.
//   Resuspend in ~250 uL PBS before permeabilization.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bsaWash1     = dispense 1 units of BSA_Solution
pbsWash1     = dispense 1 units of PBS
washBuffer1  = mix bsaWash1 with pbsWash1 for 30s
heat washBuffer1 at 25c for 3m
washedFixed  = mix fixedCells with washBuffer1 for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// IMMUNOFLUORESCENCE - STEP 3 (Paper Step 42): Permeabilize
//   cells with 0.1% v/v Triton X-100 in PBS for 1-5 min at
//   room temperature. Triton X-100 solubilizes the plasma
//   membrane to allow intracellular antibody access for
//   pan-cytokeratin (pan-CK) staining of the cytoskeleton.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tritonX100     = dispense 1 units of TritonX100
permeaCells    = mix washedFixed with tritonX100 for 3m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// IMMUNOFLUORESCENCE - STEP 4 (Paper Step 43): Wash
//   permeabilized cells with 1-2 mL PBS + 0.5% w/v BSA,
//   centrifuge at 300g for 3 min at room temperature to
//   remove Triton X-100 before antibody incubation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bsaWash2     = dispense 1 units of BSA_Solution
pbsWash2     = dispense 1 units of PBS
washBuffer2  = mix bsaWash2 with pbsWash2 for 30s
heat washBuffer2 at 25c for 3m
washedPermea = mix permeaCells with washBuffer2 for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// IMMUNOFLUORESCENCE - STEP 5 (Paper Step 44): Incubate cells
//   on ice with conjugated antibody cocktail for 30 min:
//     - FITC pan-cytokeratin (pan-CK) 1:100 -- CTC marker
//       (CK8, CK9, CK18, CK19; epithelial cytokeratins).
//       Miltenyi Biotec Asia Pacific. Excitation 490 nm,
//       emission 526 nm.
//     - APC CD45 1:100 -- leukocyte marker (WBC counter-stain
//       to exclude contaminating WBCs from CTC count).
//       Miltenyi Biotec Asia Pacific.
//     - Hoechst 33342 1:1000 (1 M stock) -- nuclear stain
//       for all nucleated cells; confirms CTC nuclei.
//   Putative CTCs: pan-CK+, CD45-, Hoechst+, round nuclei,
//   high nuclear-to-cytoplasmic (N/C) ratio.
//   Incubation on ice prevents antigen internalization and
//   non-specific binding. Model as heat at 4c for 30m.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

panCKAntibody  = dispense 1 units of PanCK_FITC_Antibody
cd45Antibody   = dispense 1 units of CD45_APC_Antibody
hoechstDye     = dispense 1 units of HoechstDye

antibodyMix    = mix panCKAntibody with cd45Antibody for 5s
fullStainMix   = mix antibodyMix with hoechstDye for 5s
stainedCells   = mix washedPermea with fullStainMix for 30m
heat stainedCells at 4c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// IMMUNOFLUORESCENCE - STEP 6 (Paper Step 45): Wash stained
//   cells with 1-2 mL PBS + 0.5% w/v BSA, centrifuge at
//   300g for 3 min to remove unbound antibody. Resuspend in
//   ~250 uL PBS and transfer to a single 96-well plate well.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bsaWash3      = dispense 1 units of BSA_Solution
pbsWash3      = dispense 1 units of PBS
washBuffer3   = mix bsaWash3 with pbsWash3 for 30s
heat washBuffer3 at 25c for 3m
washedStained = mix stainedCells with washBuffer3 for 1m

pbsFinal      = dispense 1 units of PBS
finalCells    = mix washedStained with pbsFinal for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// CTC DETECTION (Paper Step 47): Fluorescence enumeration of
//   pan-CK+/CD45-/Hoechst+ cells with round nuclei and high
//   N/C ratio. Platform: Olympus inverted microscope (IX71/81)
//   with phase-contrast, emission filters ET460/50m (Hoechst),
//   ET535/50m (pan-CK FITC), ET605/70m (CD45 APC); automated
//   stage (MetaMorph); 12-bit EM-CCD camera (Andor iXon+885).
//   Each 96-well plate well scanned in 1x1 mm grid.
//   Threshold: >7 CK+ cells per sample = positive patient.
//   Clinical range: 12-1275 CK+ breast CTCs; 10-1535 lung CTCs.
//   ctcDetection module abstracts the fluorescence readout and
//   cell classification step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ctcSignal = detect ctcDetection on finalCells for 45m

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: CTC detection gate
// Pass (BB5): ctcSignal > 0 -> pan-CK+/CD45-/Hoechst+ cells
//             enumerated above threshold (>7 CK+ cells);
//             positive patient sample confirmed. Dispose.
// Fail (BB6): ctcSignal <= 0 -> no CTCs detected above
//             threshold (healthy donor control or run failure);
//             drain stained cells.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (ctcSignal > 0) {
    dispose finalCells
} else {
    drain finalCells
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose CTC detection QC signal. Experiment ends.
// Downstream options for recovered CTCs (from inner outlet
// collected prior to staining): culture (37 C / 5% CO2),
// DNA/RNA-FISH (ALK break-apart probe, HER2/neu), KRAS
// codon 12 mutation by ICE-COLD PCR + Sanger sequencing,
// single-cell analysis. These are encoded as separate protocols.
// ============================================================

dispose ctcSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
